# ============================================================================
# STANDING RULE: every novel's `text/` folder (or per-book `text/` folders,
# for a series) holds the actual conclusive, copyrightable manuscript prose --
# as opposed to the outline/planning tables under `structure/`, which are
# fine to keep tracked. It must be gitignored (and, if it's ever accidentally
# committed with real content, untracked *and* purged from git history, not
# just removed going forward) before any real prose is written into it. This
# is a standing instruction for every future novel stamped out from
# y-template -- see y-template/structure/Dev-Road-Map/03-Phase-1-Foundations.md
# section 1.5. Do not skip this for a new novel just because it feels
# premature; add the line the same day the novel folder is created.
# ============================================================================

Streetside\ Harmonies/videos/
Streetside\ Harmonies/reference/Tesla\ Coil\ reference\ audio/
Streetside\ Harmonies/reference/reference\ images/outline-page-photos/

# Final draft text -- this is the actual copyrightable manuscript prose.
# Kept untracked/local-only until copyright has been filed; not for a public repo.
Streetside\ Harmonies/text/

# Same large-media exclusions, mirrored for the pre-migration backup snapshot
# (kept locally for safekeeping; the large media doesn't need a second git-tracked copy)
z-archive\ \(Benson\ Trio\ backup\,\ pre-Streetside-Harmonies\)/videos/
z-archive\ \(Benson\ Trio\ backup\,\ pre-Streetside-Harmonies\)/reference/Tesla\ Coil\ reference\ audio/
z-archive\ \(Benson\ Trio\ backup\,\ pre-Streetside-Harmonies\)/reference/reference\ images/outline-page-photos/
# Same reasoning as Streetside Harmonies/text/ above -- this backup snapshot
# carries its own copy of the same copyrightable manuscript prose.
z-archive\ \(Benson\ Trio\ backup\,\ pre-Streetside-Harmonies\)/text/

# Final draft text for the other novels in this repo -- same principle as
# Streetside Harmonies/text/ above, applied proactively before any of these
# have real content, so it's never an issue as they get written.
Alaska\ Rescue\ \(title\ TBD\)/text/
Colorado\ Ethics\ \(title\ TBD\)/text/
The\ Four-Realm\ Musician\ \(title\ TBD\)/text/
The\ Four-Realm\ Musician\ \(title\ TBD\)/Book\ -\ Warrior/text/
The\ Four-Realm\ Musician\ \(title\ TBD\)/Book\ -\ King/text/
The\ Four-Realm\ Musician\ \(title\ TBD\)/Book\ -\ Magician/text/
The\ Four-Realm\ Musician\ \(title\ TBD\)/Book\ -\ Lover/text/
The\ Saga\ of\ Maggie\ Aarden/text/
The\ Saga\ of\ Maggie\ Aarden/Book\ 1/text/
The\ Saga\ of\ Maggie\ Aarden/Book\ 2/text/

# InnerTepeniaGDD reference content (flattened directly into reference/, no
# longer a git submodule) -- kept untracked since it's actively evolving in
# its own separate repo; only reference/story-structure-definitions.md
# (the distilled, stable beat-structure extract) is meant to be tracked here.
reference/Dev-Road-Map/
reference/General-Overview-Notes/
reference/README.md
reference/Reference/
reference/Storyline/
reference/TODO.md
reference/Worldspace/
reference/to-be-integrated/

# Character methodology source books -- full copyrighted texts (several are
# unauthorized z-library scans), kept locally for reference but never
# committed to this public repo. The methodology files themselves
# (reference/character-methodology/methodology/) are plain tracked text and
# stay in git; only the book files under source-books/ are excluded.
reference/character-methodology/source-books/

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# worldbuilding/ -- universe-wide worldbuilding, deliberately NOT bound to any
# single novel, since every book in this line shares one universe. Two of its
# subfolders are excluded and the rest is tracked:
#
#   worldbuilding/extractions/  tracked -- our own distilled analysis
#   worldbuilding/nations/      tracked -- nation profiles, rosters, territories
#   worldbuilding/history/      tracked -- treaties, timelines, world history
#   worldbuilding/data/         IGNORED -- bulk third-party datasets
#   worldbuilding/source-books/ IGNORED -- copyrighted source texts
#
# Same principle as the character-methodology split above: what we write is
# tracked, what we merely downloaded is not.
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Copyrighted source texts used as reference for nation/region design
# (e.g. regional-culture geography works). Distilled extractions written from
# them are tracked; the book files are not.
worldbuilding/source-books/

# Bulk third-party datasets -- mineral/agricultural/energy/trade data pulled
# from USGS, FAOSTAT, EIA, Statistics Canada, INEGI, OEC and similar. These are
# large, freely re-downloadable, and not ours to redistribute. Any analysis
# written FROM them belongs in extractions/ or nations/ and stays tracked.
worldbuilding/data/

# Same reasoning, for downloaded source videos + subtitles (copyrighted media,
# not ours to redistribute) used as general story-structure craft reference --
# broader than character arcs specifically, so kept alongside
# story-structure-definitions.md rather than nested under character-methodology/.
reference/story-structure-source-videos/

# Map screenshots and hand-marked map composites kept as visual reference.
# These sit on third-party copyrighted base imagery (Google Maps and similar),
# so the images stay local. The written extraction of each one IS tracked
# (see worldbuilding/nations/*.md); the image itself is not.
**/web Screenshot*
reference/*.png
reference/*.jpg
reference/*.jpeg

*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
